<title>HUNGARY: FORECAST-HUNGARY T-BILL YIELDS SEEN CHANGING LITTLE.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-HUNGARY T-BILL YIELDS SEEN CHANGING LITTLE.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average yields on Hungary's one- and three-month discount Treasury bills were seen changing little, either upwards or downwards, at this week's auctions, a Reuter poll of dealers showed on Monday.</p>
<p>Most dealers expected the average yield on the two-year 1998/K government bonds to drop at this week's auction.</p>
<p>They saw the average yield on the three-year 1999/D bonds rising compared with the average yield on the previous three-year issue, the 1999/C bond.</p>
<p>Some dealers said that the central bank may cut its repo rates on Tuesday, which could push down the yields at Thursday's government bond auction, while other dealers believed a repo rate cut on Tuesday was not likely.</p>
<p>The Government Debt ManagementAgency will auction one-month and three-month discount Treasury bills on Tuesday and 1998/D and 1999/C bonds on Thursday.</p>
